{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541074-how-would-you-determine-the-mechanical-effect-of-magick","id":1541074,"title":"How would you determine the mechanical effect of magick?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-27T12:00:42-07:00","id":1541074,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How would you determine the mechanical effect of magick?","content":"Hello.<br /> I recently started getting a little deeper into M20, and like many others, I found myself with many questions.<br /> One of the more notable ones, is the way magick affects game systems.<br /> <br /> In M20, if we go by the <i>Dividing Successes</i> optional rule, the awakened might be able to split their successes among <i>Damage</i>, <i>Targets</i>, or <i>Duration</i>.<br /> Now while it does answer many of the combat questions, I still find it hard to understand how things like Mind Shields (Mind 1), the ability to soak Aggravated (Life 3), or increased Health Levels (also Life 3) would work.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine, told me that you go by the systems that are already available in the book, so for instance if you wanted to get a Mind Shield, you would consider it as an automatic Countermagick roll. Meaning, if a mage had their Mind Shield active and a Ventrue would try to Dominate them, the Mage would roll their Arete in order to counter the Dominate effect as a reflexive action.<br /> Now, as somebody who is relatively inexperienced in MTA, that is <i>not obvious whatsoever</i>. How could I ever guess that a Mind Shield is essentially reflexive Countermagick?<br /> <br /> Another example, would be the Aggravated soaking ability that I mentioned earlier. I was told that I should refer to the <i>Armor Chart</i> and simply treat it as armor. Now, that is a bit hard to grasp, because if somebody would simply like to harden their skin pattern after witnessing the Fortitude of a vampire, how many soaking dots would they get?<br /> <br /> Finally, since the <i>Dividing Successes</i> rule offers only <i>Damage</i>, <i>Targets</i>, and <i>Duration</i>, <u>but not</u> <i>&quot;Effect&quot;</i>, how would you determine the strength of a particular effect? That can be directly tied to the Health Levels increase that I mentioned before. Sure, you get extra Health Levels. But how many?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T03:31:03-07:00","id":1541117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541074-how-would-you-determine-the-mechanical-effect-of-magick#post1541074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello.<br /> I recently started getting a little deeper into M20, and like many others, I found myself with many questions.<br /> One of the more notable ones, is the way magick affects game systems.<br /> <br /> In M20, if we go by the <i>Dividing Successes</i> optional rule, the awakened might be able to split their successes among <i>Damage</i>, <i>Targets</i>, or <i>Duration</i>.<br /> Now while it does answer many of the combat questions, I still find it hard to understand how things like Mind Shields (Mind 1), the ability to soak Aggravated (Life 3), or increased Health Levels (also Life 3) would work.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine, told me that you go by the systems that are already available in the book, so for instance if you wanted to get a Mind Shield, you would consider it as an automatic Countermagick roll. Meaning, if a mage had their Mind Shield active and a Ventrue would try to Dominate them, the Mage would roll their Arete in order to counter the Dominate effect as a reflexive action.<br /> Now, as somebody who is relatively inexperienced in MTA, that is <i>not obvious whatsoever</i>. How could I ever guess that a Mind Shield is essentially reflexive Countermagick?<br /> <br /> Another example, would be the Aggravated soaking ability that I mentioned earlier. I was told that I should refer to the <i>Armor Chart</i> and simply treat it as armor. Now, that is a bit hard to grasp, because if somebody would simply like to harden their skin pattern after witnessing the Fortitude of a vampire, how many soaking dots would they get?<br /> <br /> Finally, since the <i>Dividing Successes</i> rule offers only <i>Damage</i>, <i>Targets</i>, and <i>Duration</i>, <u>but not</u> <i>&quot;Effect&quot;</i>, how would you determine the strength of a particular effect? That can be directly tied to the Health Levels increase that I mentioned before. Sure, you get extra Health Levels. But how many?</div> </div> </div> </div>In case of mind shield you do not roll, its an automatic soak of successes done by the attacker (page 519).<br /> As for soaking agrrovative damage. Its not an extra dice pool. It just allows you to use your stamina to soak aggrovative damage like you would with bashing.<br /> As for effects use feats of magic chart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T16:30:50-07:00","id":1541143,"title":"","content":"In MtAs, the way a magic effect works is whatever makes sense for the character's beliefs and how it was done. That's a staple of the game: there are no wrong mechanics, as long as they do what was planned.<br /> <br /> The strength of an effect is also a very open matter, it is entirely in the hands of the ST to adjudicate based on the Feats of Magic chart. If you want more concrete rules you can go for the Revised core book, but if you can't, don't sweat it.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, 1 success = 1 whatever isn't a bad starting point, although you may want extra successes to start things out or at certain thresholds.<br /> <br /> Extra Health Boxes? 1 per success. Extra soak? 1 per success. Extra attributes? Skills? 1 per success. Limbs? I'd say 5 for the first, then 1 per success.<br /> <br /> What gives it a semblance of balance is the Duration chart and the limits on concentration. No matter how incredible an effect, by itself it's just a turn. Other than that, ask for more successes if you think you need, but otherwise don't fret too much: Mage is about too much power.<br /> <br /> For your examples, I'd give the following suggestions:<br /> <br /> 1- Extra Health: 1 to 1, starting at the Bruised level and going down as they increase. To move one box up I'd ask for an extra success;<br /> <br /> 2- Soaking Agg: 2+ successes with Life to make your own Stamina do it, but if you want armor of some kind it's 1 to 1 as usual. The + is just in case you want a grittier game;<br /> <br /> 3- Mind Shield: it's not <i>exactly </i>Countermagic, but close. Any mind effect must subtract the strength of the shield, so if you have a shield with 3 successes on potency, then any attempt at Dominate loses the first 3 successes.<br /> <br /> 4- Optionally, if you don't want to place successes on Duration, your Mind Shield may be ablative, so successes on mind effects degrade the shield, but it has no duration limit.<br /> <br /> All of those effects target someone, so you can ask for an extra success to target others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T18:09:22-07:00","id":1541312,"title":"","content":"Well, Momteparnas basically said it all.<br /> <br /> What I always like to add is that &quot;quick dirty Magik&quot; is usually rather... Weak. I mean, you start with Arete 3, what is it that you can actually do in a single turn with that? Let's assume a simple Heal spell for instance (Life 3), that's already dif 6 if it is Coincidental (which in this case, most likely would not), meaning that your average amount of successes will be 1 and half. Thus meaning that a lot of times you'll only get a single success.<br /> <br /> That's why it is often said that &quot;Mages are the most powerful splat... When they are prepared&quot;.<br /> <br /> What that means is... Rituals.<br /> <br /> This means that your Mage will most of the time be walking around with a bunch of cool tricks that are &quot;always on&quot; (check that part about duration &quot;permanent&quot;).<br /> <br /> In fact, it is possible - and perhaps, even highly recommended - that you actually &quot;exchange&quot; your ability to &quot;wave Magik&quot; for some potent perma-effects - meaning, getting so many simultaneous effects that it becomes practically impossible to try new ones due to difficulty.<br /> <br /> Thus, instead of getting a single soaking level of mental shield and &quot;wasting&quot; a turn with your only single possible Magik on that, you just build a powerful 10 points mental shield at the comfort of your Sanctum (spending 10 successes on that in a prolonged ritual) plus any amount of successes required to extend the duration of the effect - it's not really necessary to make it be &quot;permanent&quot;, but at the very least you would like it to be for something like 6 months. But even extending your rituals to last for a single day is good most of the time - it simply means that you always have to &quot;renew your prayers&quot; every single morning after getting off the bed.<br /> <br /> Just take into consideration things like Permadox and Pattern Bleeding and you're pretty much good to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}